application  choupoSolve;

//  AUDIENCE.  A SHOWCASE composes engineering (bin/curate/check_case_tiers):
//  three kinetic catalyst beds with interbed waste-heat boilers inside two
//  recycle cuts, every exchanger designed by Kern, and an appraisal are a
//  plant at one design stage, not a feature being isolated.

tier         showcase;
description  "Green ammonia, 1200 t/day, BASIC DESIGN (illustrated design stage FEL-3, process side; rung 3 of the green-ammonia sequence): the PEQ 2026-27 base case with its Gibbs converter replaced by three adiabatic catalyst beds on the Dyson-Simon (1968) rate law for an iron catalyst, two interbed coolers raising HP steam (a declared credit), and the feed/effluent exchanger preheating bed 1 against bed 3. Every exchanger is designed by the Kern method; the three bed volumes are SOLVED by the engine (a DesignSpec on the outlet temperature and the approach to equilibrium) and the beds sized from them with a declared catalyst charge; Turton costing and a DCF, still a study-type estimate.";
verbosity    3;

reports
{
    streamTable   {}
    massBalance   {}
    energyBalance {}
    computed      {}
    spreadsheet   {}
    design        {}     // reports/design/sizing.csv: every sized item, the relief valves included
}
